cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CyberSWISS: Enterprise Security Audit & Remediation Platform"
message: "If you use CyberSWISS in your work, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The CyberSWISS Contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/jomardyan/CyberSWISS-Cybersecurity-Scan-Win-Linux"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jomardyan/CyberSWISS-Cybersecurity-Scan-Win-Linux"
url: "https://github.com/jomardyan/CyberSWISS-Cybersecurity-Scan-Win-Linux"
abstract: >-
  CyberSWISS is a cross-platform security audit, hardening and compliance
  scanner for Linux servers, Windows endpoints, and Active Directory
  environments. It provides 66 agentless audit scripts (33 Bash and 33
  PowerShell) covering system hardening, CIS baseline checks, vulnerability
  and CVE scanning, secrets detection, SAST/SCA, infrastructure-as-code
  scanning, and SOC 2 / HIPAA / GDPR compliance mapping, together with a
  Python orchestrator, REST API, SQLite scan history with drift detection,
  accepted-risk baselines, and SARIF output for CI/CD security gates.
keywords:
  - security-audit
  - security-scanner
  - compliance
  - hardening
  - cis-benchmark
  - vulnerability-scanner
  - devsecops
  - sarif
  - linux
  - windows
  - powershell
  - bash
